                <pb facs="0121" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/1372: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-16T11:00:00+03:00">January 16, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 16—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Japanese Chargé d’Affaires informs me that he has received long and favorable
                    telegraphic instructions from his Government relative to the Chinese Eastern
                    Railway negotiations. He thinks chances are excellent that sale will be
                    consummated within 6 weeks.</p>
                <p>In reply to a query he categorically denied that there was any substance to
                    current rumors that a nonaggression pact was also probable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
